notes: >
  A test-timeout override must be rendered into `go test -timeout` as well as the gate's own
  timeout, or the tool would be killed before it could print its diagnosis. --plan --json shows the
  effective argv, and this fixture asserts it: the gate carries the 90s override while `go test`
  is rendered at 81s (90%), so Go prints its own goroutine dump before the runner kills it.
requires: [go]
argv: ['--all', '--plan', '--json']
exitCode: 0
outputIncludes:
  - '-timeout=81s'
  - '"timeoutMs": 90000'
